{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1456675-question-about-keys","id":1456675,"title":"Question about Keys","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-12T09:07:34-07:00","id":1456675,"title":"Question about Keys","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> There is something I\u2019m a little confused about. On p. 121 of the Geist core book, in the section about Keys, it states that\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201c Multiple Unlocks: Characters may only unlock a Haunt with one Key at a time. They may unlock a Haunt with multiple instances of the same Key, but only the free Plasm and the Doomed Condition stack.\u201d<br /> <br /> For some reason, I\u2019m having trouble understanding this rule wording. Is this saying that I can activate a single Haunt with multiple instances of the same Key simultaneously? For instance, unlocking one use of the Caul with three Keys of Chance.<br /> <br /> If so, how does this differ from having several different Keys? Unlocking a Key is a reflexive action. I don\u2019t see much mechanical difference between unlocking three of the same Key in a single turn, and three entirely different Keys in a single turn.<br /> <br /> Is there any benefit to having multiple instances of the same Key, as opposed to having several different Keys? The only potential benefit that I can see is that you can claim the Memento Collector condition if you have at least five Mementos of the same Key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","user":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","date":". 08-12-2021, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T10:38:33-07:00","id":1456681,"title":"","content":"Yes, if you have the Key of Chance thrice for whatever reason, you could use all three to unlock the Caul at the same time. In return, you would add Dexterity to your Unlock roll, gain (Dexterity x 3) Plasm, and suffer three versions of the Doomed (Chance) Condition. You could not unlock the Caul with both the Key of Chance and the Key of Beasts, however. The main reason for this interdiction, I believe, is to prevent Attribute confusion.<br /> <br /> The main benefit of having the same Key multiple times is the ability to utilize it while Doomed. For instance, if your Geist has the Key of Chance and you also have a Memento with the Key of Chance, you could use one, become Doomed, then use the other. Otherwise you'd have to resolve the Doomed Condition before you could use that specific instance again. In this way, a Sin-Eater can specialize in one Attribute rather than spreading yourself out. Is that putting all your eggs in one basket? Sure. But what's a second life without a few risks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}